claude.toml, codex.toml, opencode.toml and pi.toml are verbatim copies of
src/detect/manifests/ at this revision. Their inline comments remain intact.
These files contain no additional copyright or license notices.

The evaluator in zellij-utils/src/harness_map/evaluator.rs ports
src/detect/manifest.rs. Changes: pure public API, no filesystem or remote
cache, string manifest versions with upstream format validation, explicit
unsupported-engine errors,
serializable results and unknown-label handling. Matcher gates, regions,
priority ties, validation limits and known-agent idle fallback remain intact.
Herdr does not distinguish questions from permissions; both remain blocked.

The region fixtures in evaluator.rs copy the upstream test
screen_regions_extract_structure_without_classifying_agent_state from
src/detect/manifest/tests.rs, with formatting changes. These are synthetic
test inputs.
fixtures.toml contains local synthetic harness screens, except the pi
Working... string also occurs in upstream tests/cross_area.rs.
The evaluator also accepts a local question state for supplemental manifests.
Local supplemental TOML and synthetic screens live beside this directory in
local/. They are fork additions, not modified herdr manifests or captured screens.
